WEBVTT

00:12.053 --> 00:14.389
♪ See the daylight ♪

00:15.223 --> 00:17.392
♪ Covering the sky ♪

00:18.852 --> 00:22.230
♪ Hear the wind say ♪

00:22.313 --> 00:26.484
♪ No matter what you do, my friend ♪

00:26.568 --> 00:29.195
♪ You know the world
Still needs your light ♪

00:29.279 --> 00:32.449
♪ Let it just shine ♪

00:32.532 --> 00:34.951
♪ You'll be free ♪

00:35.035 --> 00:38.121
♪ From all the things you used to be ♪

00:40.040 --> 00:42.042
[bell clanging]

00:47.756 --> 00:51.634
DOONA!

01:02.270 --> 01:03.605
Who is that guy? Talk to me.

01:16.242 --> 01:17.452
Stay with me.

01:26.044 --> 01:28.046
[mysterious music playing]

02:00.703 --> 02:01.663
Let's get going.

02:22.350 --> 02:23.560
[car engine starts]

02:45.206 --> 02:48.126
EPISODE 7
CLEAR THE AIR

03:01.598 --> 03:02.557
Why are you here?

03:06.019 --> 03:07.187
Are you feeling sick?

03:16.821 --> 03:18.781
You're getting hot. It might be a fever.

03:19.949 --> 03:20.909
[Doona sighs]

03:22.410 --> 03:24.329
Is there something you want to say to me?

03:25.121 --> 03:27.749
Shouldn't you be the one
who has something to say to me?

03:30.877 --> 03:32.086
Let's talk when we're in Seoul.

03:37.425 --> 03:38.760
Your career's on the line.

03:38.843 --> 03:41.054
It's time to fix it
before the world forgets you.

03:41.638 --> 03:43.556
And what if I want to be forgotten?

03:45.350 --> 03:46.351
Both by you

03:47.101 --> 03:48.353
and by the public.

03:48.978 --> 03:51.481
What do you think you'll do
with your career if I told you that?

03:55.485 --> 03:56.694
I know you're just saying that,

03:57.612 --> 03:59.489
because I know what it is
you fear the most.

04:00.073 --> 04:02.283
Being forgotten and ending up all alone.

04:05.662 --> 04:06.871
So that's why you did it.

04:08.248 --> 04:10.375
Dumped me in that house all by myself

04:10.458 --> 04:12.627
and didn't bother
to come visit me even once…

04:15.213 --> 04:17.215
making me realize
what abandonment feels like.

04:19.259 --> 04:21.594
I quit, so you punished me. Is that it?

04:30.061 --> 04:31.145
[exhales shakily]

04:34.482 --> 04:35.400
I want out.

04:37.277 --> 04:38.403
Let me out of the car.

04:41.364 --> 04:42.782
I said I want out!

04:42.865 --> 04:44.784
I said stop the car!

04:44.867 --> 04:47.036
[panting]

04:49.038 --> 04:50.081
Hey, stop it.

04:51.666 --> 04:54.168
- I want out!
- I said stop it, Lee Doona!

04:54.252 --> 04:57.171
- [Doona screams]
- [In-wook] Would you stop it?

04:58.756 --> 05:00.758
[dramatic music playing]

05:02.093 --> 05:03.094
[Doona yelps]

05:14.564 --> 05:16.190
- What do you think you're doing?
- Get away!

05:18.484 --> 05:19.944
Let go of me!

05:21.654 --> 05:23.323
Get away!

05:24.032 --> 05:25.116
[crying]

05:26.117 --> 05:27.201
Stop this now.

05:28.536 --> 05:29.787
Get ahold of yourself.

05:31.456 --> 05:32.874
[crying]

05:33.458 --> 05:34.834
That's enough! Stop, Doona!

05:43.092 --> 05:44.552
So I bet this was fun, huh?

05:45.261 --> 05:46.679
It made you feel good, huh?

05:47.180 --> 05:50.475
Because of you, I felt so alone
and like I was drowning every day.

05:52.560 --> 05:53.644
Don't be so dramatic.

05:53.728 --> 05:56.189
You're worse than my mother,
you narcissistic ass!

05:57.231 --> 05:59.025
You knew I liked you, and

05:59.692 --> 06:02.820
how desperate I was to see you,
and you just left me there.

06:04.197 --> 06:06.616
You manipulated me
and took me for granted, huh?

06:07.784 --> 06:09.911
I despise you, you fucking asshole.

06:13.331 --> 06:14.248
[whimpering]

06:15.750 --> 06:18.628
You and I know you didn't wait for me
because you had feelings.

06:20.380 --> 06:21.756
You always make a mess of things,

06:21.839 --> 06:24.217
and you always expect me
to fix it for you.

06:24.300 --> 06:25.927
You need a ticket back into this industry,

06:26.010 --> 06:27.553
and you know I'm that ticket.

06:27.637 --> 06:29.055
Tell me I'm wrong, huh?

06:31.474 --> 06:34.435
You actually think you really know
what it means to be in love, Doona?

06:36.646 --> 06:38.773
If you really did care at all for me,

06:38.856 --> 06:42.485
then you wouldn't have left us out to dry
and blown up everything we worked for.

06:42.568 --> 06:44.278
You're the reason the tour ended.

06:45.738 --> 06:47.740
Don't act like you're the victim here.
We are.

06:48.408 --> 06:50.076
I didn't use you, Lee Doona!

06:50.159 --> 06:52.036
It's the other way around, all right?

06:52.954 --> 06:55.706
You're the person who used us
to further your career, huh?

06:56.624 --> 06:58.042
You neglected yourself.

06:58.626 --> 07:00.169
[crying]

07:03.673 --> 07:05.007
You're a complete mess.

07:08.052 --> 07:10.680
Even still, you have no problem
messing up your life.

07:12.807 --> 07:14.225
[crying]

07:15.518 --> 07:17.520
[somber music playing]

07:22.150 --> 07:24.444
[sobbing]

07:55.725 --> 07:56.684
[sighs]

08:02.648 --> 08:03.774
RECENTS

08:03.858 --> 08:05.067
LEE DOONA

08:06.277 --> 08:07.612
[line ringing]

08:20.917 --> 08:21.834
[In-wook] Yes.

08:22.627 --> 08:26.923
Yeah, you're right. It is today.
Well, there's been a bit of an incident.

08:28.716 --> 08:30.176
[woman] Miss Lee Doona's guardian?

08:30.676 --> 08:31.511
[In-wook] Yes.

08:32.303 --> 08:34.722
No, no, I'll…
I'll be there today for sure.

08:35.640 --> 08:36.641
Yes, but

08:37.600 --> 08:39.268
do we really need to decide now?

08:40.394 --> 08:43.105
Yes. I'll get there later tonight.

08:44.690 --> 08:47.568
Okay. Don't forget to look
into that hospital I mentioned.

08:48.736 --> 08:50.196
- Okay.
- [phone vibrating]

08:55.826 --> 08:59.539
LEE WON-JUN

09:15.137 --> 09:17.139
[tender music playing]

09:28.317 --> 09:29.360
[line ringing]

09:32.697 --> 09:33.739
[sighs]

09:37.118 --> 09:37.952
[Doona sniffles]

09:38.035 --> 09:39.203
[shivers]

09:43.207 --> 09:45.835
You have
this really great relationship with her,

09:46.669 --> 09:48.588
'cause you've known her so long.

09:49.171 --> 09:51.257
That's why I'm very jealous of you.

09:51.340 --> 09:52.758
These aren't mine.

09:57.138 --> 09:58.889
[In-wook] You've gotten better at lying.

09:59.390 --> 10:01.267
Stop contacting me and wait quietly.

10:29.086 --> 10:30.671
[clattering]

10:33.633 --> 10:34.717
[whimpers]

10:39.305 --> 10:40.264
[sighs]

10:43.893 --> 10:44.894
[phone chimes]

10:45.645 --> 10:48.189
RECEIVED TWO TICKETS
FOR TODAY'S LAST BUS TO SEOUL

11:02.370 --> 11:04.246
[phone ringing]

11:05.331 --> 11:06.499
MOM

11:28.145 --> 11:30.856
Get in the car,
unless you plan to never see me again.

11:32.733 --> 11:34.485
I used to fear words like that.

11:36.070 --> 11:38.489
Now your words
somehow no longer scare me at all.

11:41.492 --> 11:42.952
Well, do what you want, then.

11:43.035 --> 11:45.162
You won't see my face
from now on, you got it?

11:51.419 --> 11:52.753
What was the point, then?

11:52.837 --> 11:54.547
Why did you come to the showcase?

12:01.345 --> 12:02.179
[inhales shakily]

12:04.265 --> 12:05.891
[somber music playing]

12:55.566 --> 12:59.528
KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE

13:04.200 --> 13:07.745
Jeez, bro. Slow down.
What's up with you? You good?

13:11.290 --> 13:13.459
Why is everything hard for me?

13:15.795 --> 13:16.629
[scoffs]

13:16.712 --> 13:19.298
You know what's easy and simple? Math.

13:19.882 --> 13:22.301
[scoffs] It's only easy for you, dickhead.

13:23.636 --> 13:24.804
[chuckles]

13:25.679 --> 13:27.473
[Kooksu slurps] Ah.

13:31.060 --> 13:33.270
Who do celebrities date usually?
I have no idea.

13:33.354 --> 13:34.980
Hmm? Who?

13:37.399 --> 13:38.317
Oh.

13:38.984 --> 13:41.612
I guess they date someone like themselves.

13:42.279 --> 13:43.906
Others at the top of their game.

13:45.491 --> 13:47.993
But… if I were Doona…

13:48.077 --> 13:49.078
[exhales]

13:49.161 --> 13:50.663
…Son Heung-min would be the guy.

13:50.746 --> 13:53.332
Oh wow! You see his free kick yesterday?

13:53.415 --> 13:55.292
The way he curved it was crazy.

13:55.376 --> 13:58.170
His is not the foot of a mere mortal.
No way, man.

13:58.254 --> 14:00.256
And I was a fan of Messi's
for the longest time.

14:00.339 --> 14:02.800
- But now it's Son Heung-min all the way.
- [sighs]

14:06.262 --> 14:08.264
[emotional music playing]

15:00.482 --> 15:02.776
RECENTS
LEE WON-JUN

15:23.213 --> 15:25.132
RECENTS
LEE WON-JUN

15:38.395 --> 15:39.396
[sighs]

15:43.567 --> 15:47.071
What was the point, then?
Why did you come to the showcase?

15:47.154 --> 15:49.156
[pop music playing]

16:17.518 --> 16:18.936
[In-wook] You dance, don't you?

16:19.019 --> 16:20.354
LEE DOONA

16:20.437 --> 16:22.064
[pop music continues]

16:25.651 --> 16:26.694
You in eighth grade?

16:27.903 --> 16:28.946
[Doona scoffs]

16:29.989 --> 16:32.616
[In-wook] All you have to do
is follow my directions.

16:32.700 --> 16:35.369
As long as you do,
you'll have nothing to worry about.

16:36.161 --> 16:38.580
Once you sign with us,
I'll take care of everything for you,

16:38.664 --> 16:40.749
where you stay, what you eat,

16:40.833 --> 16:42.126
even what you wear.

16:43.252 --> 16:46.088
But in return,
you can't ever keep anything from me.

16:46.672 --> 16:47.756
If you do, we're done.

16:48.924 --> 16:50.467
[Doona] And why should I do that?

16:52.886 --> 16:55.180
Are we gonna be
like a family or something?

16:55.264 --> 16:56.432
[In-wook] Something like that.

16:57.683 --> 16:59.810
If that makes it easier
for you to understand.

16:59.893 --> 17:00.894
[music stops]

17:10.863 --> 17:11.697
[sighs]

17:33.260 --> 17:34.219
Does it hurt here?

17:37.514 --> 17:38.724
How about here?

17:51.820 --> 17:53.363
That's enough for today.

18:06.919 --> 18:07.878
[door closes]

18:14.927 --> 18:17.096
Mmm! This place is good, right?

18:17.179 --> 18:18.263
Mmm!

18:18.347 --> 18:19.181
Ah!

18:22.226 --> 18:23.060
Ah!

18:24.228 --> 18:25.395
[I-ra laughs]

18:25.479 --> 18:26.897
It's insanely good!

18:26.980 --> 18:28.107
[door beeps]

18:28.190 --> 18:29.066
[groans]

18:30.400 --> 18:33.362
Oh. Ah, the house feels so empty.

18:33.445 --> 18:34.363
Doesn't it?

18:40.369 --> 18:41.495
Yun-taek.

18:41.578 --> 18:43.205
- [Yun-taek] Yeah?
- Uh…

18:43.872 --> 18:46.542
- The other day there was this person--
- Who? A chick?

18:48.210 --> 18:49.253
Uh, no, it's just,

18:49.336 --> 18:52.798
I was with a friend and, well,
they kept acting happy around me.

18:52.881 --> 18:55.425
They would, uh… shake like this.

18:55.509 --> 18:57.719
Why do you think that person
keeps popping inside my head?

18:58.554 --> 19:01.348
- What are you trying to say?
- [Jeong-hun] Uh…

19:02.599 --> 19:04.143
[phone ringing]

19:05.060 --> 19:06.520
CHOI I-RA

19:10.899 --> 19:12.901
[curious music playing]

19:24.204 --> 19:25.080
[clears throat]

19:28.333 --> 19:30.460
Huh. Well, hi! [chuckles]

19:30.544 --> 19:31.670
Hey.

19:31.753 --> 19:32.754
[I-ra] You got here fast.

19:33.338 --> 19:35.007
- [Jeong-hun] You look busy.
- Oh, is…

19:35.090 --> 19:36.341
- [Jeong-hun] Mmm.
- Aw, seriously?

19:36.425 --> 19:38.552
How did you know I was thirsty?
Thank you.

19:38.635 --> 19:39.553
[Jeong-hun] Mm-hmm.

19:41.054 --> 19:42.431
[I-ra] Mmm!

19:42.514 --> 19:43.807
So refreshing! Mmm!

19:47.102 --> 19:48.812
What did you need help with?
You didn't say.

19:49.521 --> 19:50.439
[I-ra] Mmm.

19:51.315 --> 19:53.192
Our department's doing a fashion show.

19:53.817 --> 19:55.402
You don't need to model on stage,

19:55.485 --> 19:57.237
but could you please
help me with the fitting?

19:57.321 --> 19:59.615
I'll buy dinner afterwards.
Please help, hmm?

20:00.199 --> 20:01.200
[Jeong-hun] Hmm…

20:02.075 --> 20:03.160
That's a yes!

20:03.744 --> 20:06.413
Okay, first,
can you just try this on for me?

20:06.496 --> 20:07.331
Here you go.

20:07.414 --> 20:08.832
You can change right over there,

20:08.916 --> 20:10.918
and if you need me,
I'll help you put it on as well.

20:11.001 --> 20:11.835
[Jeong-hun] Huh?

20:12.502 --> 20:13.670
Okay…

20:16.673 --> 20:18.008
[exhales]

20:24.848 --> 20:25.766
[grunts softly]

20:32.439 --> 20:33.273
Hmm?

20:34.066 --> 20:35.901
[I-ra yelling indistinctly in Portuguese]

20:35.984 --> 20:39.112
[in Portuguese] Let me ask you this!
How could you do that so easily?

20:39.196 --> 20:42.616
That is definitely not true, I-ra.
I've never once given up on you.

20:42.699 --> 20:44.284
My heart has always been yours.

20:44.368 --> 20:45.661
[in English] Oh, give me a break.

20:45.744 --> 20:48.121
[in Portuguese] I've finally realized

20:48.205 --> 20:50.832
that you're the only woman in my life.

20:50.916 --> 20:51.917
[in English] Hey!

20:53.252 --> 20:55.462
What's wrong?
Did you run out of money again?

20:56.421 --> 20:57.256
Just so you know,

20:57.339 --> 21:00.050
now I'm into someone
else who isn't completely insane, huh?

21:00.676 --> 21:01.677
[Jeong-hun] Hey, babe.

21:02.719 --> 21:04.096
[upbeat music playing]

21:24.658 --> 21:27.119
Can you take a look at this
and see if it's right?

21:27.202 --> 21:28.036
I wasn't sure.

21:28.120 --> 21:29.121
Oh…

21:30.914 --> 21:32.541
- Okay.
- I-ra.

21:35.544 --> 21:38.088
[in Portuguese]
Don't do this, I-ra. Let's start over.

21:38.171 --> 21:40.382
[in English] What are you doing?
Ow, that hurts! Ow!

21:40.465 --> 21:41.550
[in Portuguese] Please.

21:45.721 --> 21:48.056
[in English] You're gonna pay my girl back
every damn penny.

21:48.140 --> 21:50.809
And don't touch her again
if you'd like to walk out of here alive.

21:50.892 --> 21:52.894
[rock music playing]

21:53.937 --> 21:56.815
[squeals] The sweet smell of money!

21:56.898 --> 21:59.067
Whoo! [chuckles]

21:59.151 --> 22:01.320
Smell it. Ah!

22:01.403 --> 22:03.613
Ah! [chuckles]

22:03.697 --> 22:05.741
Oh yeah! Come on! Come on!

22:05.824 --> 22:06.742
Oh!

22:06.825 --> 22:08.452
- Aw, do it. Do it again.
- [Jeong-hun sighs]

22:08.535 --> 22:09.411
Aw, yeah!

22:09.995 --> 22:11.330
- Aw!
- [chuckles]

22:12.706 --> 22:13.749
[I-ra] Okay, last one!

22:13.832 --> 22:14.666
[chuckles]

22:27.929 --> 22:29.473
[somber music playing]

22:34.144 --> 22:35.312
[sighs]

22:52.871 --> 22:53.705
Hello there.

23:00.629 --> 23:02.506
Just getting back from visiting home?

23:04.424 --> 23:06.510
- Yeah.
- That's great.

23:08.178 --> 23:09.596
When's your next break?

23:09.679 --> 23:11.098
Wanna take a week vacation?

23:12.224 --> 23:14.434
We could go all the way to Shanghai

23:14.518 --> 23:15.936
or maybe Japan?

23:16.645 --> 23:17.562
Or Guam?

23:18.146 --> 23:19.022
[sighs]

23:22.776 --> 23:23.735
When did you return?

23:23.819 --> 23:24.861
Just this morning.

23:26.738 --> 23:27.572
How's your cold?

23:27.656 --> 23:28.657
It's okay now.

23:31.535 --> 23:32.577
That's good to hear.

23:34.121 --> 23:35.956
I'm tired. I'm going inside.

23:36.039 --> 23:36.873
[Doona] Hey,

23:37.457 --> 23:38.834
say what's been bothering you.

23:41.545 --> 23:44.005
Just speak your mind
and stop being so frustrating.

23:46.800 --> 23:49.344
If I say what I want to,
I might say something I'll regret later.

23:49.428 --> 23:50.720
Go ahead. Say it anyway.

23:50.804 --> 23:53.014
Even if you might regret it,
I'm willing to hear you out.

23:55.684 --> 24:00.397
Go on, ask me… if we did anything.
It's what you wanna know, am I right?

24:00.480 --> 24:01.898
- What?
- What, it isn't?

24:01.982 --> 24:04.860
Come on, you were imagining
a lot of things, weren't you?

24:04.943 --> 24:07.320
Or is it because you
don't have the balls to get angry?

24:08.697 --> 24:10.824
Wow, so much for you saying you're sorry.

24:12.534 --> 24:14.578
Do you even feel bad for what you did?

24:15.078 --> 24:17.539
Well, what right do I have
to get mad at you?

24:17.622 --> 24:20.333
I have no say at all
what happens between the two of you.

24:21.001 --> 24:23.128
I just want to know
what you're doing with me right now.

24:23.712 --> 24:25.630
I thought it wouldn't matter to me

24:25.714 --> 24:29.342
if you were just having a little fun
or taking a break or feeling lonely.

24:29.843 --> 24:31.845
I liked you,
and I thought I could handle it.

24:31.928 --> 24:33.597
I didn't care
if you had no feelings for me.

24:33.680 --> 24:36.057
[somber music playing]

24:38.101 --> 24:40.020
And now I know
I can't handle this anymore.

24:41.730 --> 24:43.607
I get why I wouldn't be your type,

24:43.690 --> 24:45.317
'cause I'm just some guy.

24:52.073 --> 24:53.825
You just left me there by myself.

24:54.743 --> 24:56.203
You take everything too far.

25:01.374 --> 25:02.292
[I-ra] Oh!

25:07.297 --> 25:08.298
[door beeps]

25:08.381 --> 25:09.299
[door opens]

25:12.052 --> 25:12.886
[door closes]

25:12.969 --> 25:13.929
[door beeps]

25:18.308 --> 25:19.684
Hey, wait, Won-jun.

25:19.768 --> 25:21.645
You're staying here
over winter break, right?

25:21.728 --> 25:22.854
Our landlady was asking us.

25:22.938 --> 25:26.274
Actually, I'm moving out.
I better give her notice, then.

25:28.318 --> 25:30.237
What? Are you serious?

25:30.820 --> 25:31.738
Why?

25:46.628 --> 25:47.504
[sighs]

25:50.674 --> 25:51.550
[door closes]

25:55.011 --> 25:56.555
[somber music playing]

25:56.638 --> 25:57.806
[sighs]

26:02.435 --> 26:03.270
[sighs]

26:17.158 --> 26:18.535
[gate squeaks]

26:24.958 --> 26:27.252
[In-wook] Yes,
I'm doing my best to sort things out.

26:27.335 --> 26:29.379
Yes, I'll update you
as soon as I have news.

26:29.462 --> 26:30.380
I apologize for this.

26:45.562 --> 26:46.396
Why'd you do it?

26:48.732 --> 26:49.649
Lee Doona.

26:54.654 --> 26:55.530
[sighs]

26:58.199 --> 26:59.993
I'm sure I told you already.

27:03.038 --> 27:04.914
I can't sing. I just can't anymore.

27:08.793 --> 27:09.711
All right then.

27:10.920 --> 27:12.088
Take a break for now.

27:24.100 --> 27:25.268
[phone vibrating]

27:39.366 --> 27:40.659
Yes, President Ma.

27:41.743 --> 27:42.702
It's not happening.

27:43.203 --> 27:45.705
We're pulling Doona out.
It'll be a four-person group.

27:46.206 --> 27:47.123
I'm sorry.

27:48.041 --> 27:49.209
[somber music playing]

28:20.198 --> 28:21.324
[woman] Welcome.

28:42.512 --> 28:43.430
[clears throat]

28:55.775 --> 28:57.110
You can't be serious.

28:57.736 --> 28:59.779
[scoffs] So you
really have given up on singing.

28:59.863 --> 29:00.780
Why not?

29:02.031 --> 29:03.575
I sleep when I want to,

29:03.658 --> 29:05.076
eat whatever I want to,

29:05.160 --> 29:06.536
and sit around doing nothing.

29:07.162 --> 29:08.329
Did you enjoy it, then?

29:09.497 --> 29:11.249
Watching us crash and burn like that?

29:12.292 --> 29:14.544
I knew you would think that, but no.

29:15.503 --> 29:16.755
You should've had more success.

29:18.131 --> 29:19.090
Tell me about it.

29:20.800 --> 29:23.094
At the time, I would've loved
shoving that in your face.

29:24.846 --> 29:25.889
[Doona sighs]

29:29.225 --> 29:30.143
I remember

29:31.603 --> 29:33.730
you said
you couldn't sing at all that day.

29:35.273 --> 29:36.232
I believe you, Doona.

29:39.569 --> 29:40.820
And I did back then too.

29:42.530 --> 29:43.364
[sighs]

29:43.907 --> 29:45.283
I know we weren't always

29:46.284 --> 29:47.952
the greatest group members or friends,

29:49.037 --> 29:51.206
But we were supposed
to be in this together.

29:53.082 --> 29:54.584
So we all understand.

29:56.336 --> 29:58.296
To be honest,
I was thinking you'd feel resentful.

29:59.464 --> 30:01.591
If you hadn't done what you did back then,

30:02.675 --> 30:03.843
I would have soon enough.

30:05.929 --> 30:06.763
[sighs]

30:10.099 --> 30:11.518
You know I don't actually

30:12.602 --> 30:13.436
hate you, right?

30:16.022 --> 30:18.608
I just wanted to be like you,
and I couldn't at all.

30:20.318 --> 30:22.362
And I didn't want to hate myself for it,

30:23.655 --> 30:25.740
so that's why I always hated you instead.

30:37.210 --> 30:38.294
[Doona sighs]

30:38.378 --> 30:39.921
10 YEARS LATER GROUND

30:48.054 --> 30:49.264
[register beeping]

30:50.932 --> 30:51.975
[register whirs]

30:53.393 --> 30:55.562
[Won-jun] Sorry,
we're closed for the night.

31:01.609 --> 31:03.444
I left a few things
in the drawer the other day.

31:03.528 --> 31:04.988
Oh, okay.

31:05.697 --> 31:06.739
Well, come on in, then.

31:25.049 --> 31:27.051
- Sorry, could you move?
- Oh. Oh, sure.

31:38.730 --> 31:40.982
[emotional music playing]

31:49.866 --> 31:51.701
So are you still living in a studio?

31:52.744 --> 31:54.954
No, I found an apartment a few days ago.

31:55.038 --> 31:58.416
It's little far from school, though,
but I like it a lot.

31:58.499 --> 32:01.419
And it's definitely way better than having
to commute from my parents' home.

32:02.253 --> 32:03.254
Glad to hear that.

32:05.256 --> 32:08.259
How does it feel to be dating now?
Are you happy?

32:14.349 --> 32:17.185
I wanted to give you and Doona some space.

32:18.645 --> 32:20.063
You're different with her.

32:20.605 --> 32:22.649
It's a side of you
I've never seen, you know?

32:23.483 --> 32:25.360
She brings out a whole new Won-Jun.

32:26.903 --> 32:28.112
[Jin-ju chuckles]

32:28.196 --> 32:29.781
Hey.

32:29.864 --> 32:32.241
Just for the record,
I think it's a good change for you.

32:33.910 --> 32:35.662
Hey, I'm being serious.

32:36.788 --> 32:38.790
Lee Won-jun, head over heels.

32:38.873 --> 32:40.959
- That's a rare thing to see.
- [chuckles]

32:42.335 --> 32:43.419
[Jin-ju chuckles]

32:45.421 --> 32:46.714
[phones chime]

32:48.216 --> 32:51.886
[I-ra] You are invited to
my Samba Party of Unity and Forgiveness!

32:51.970 --> 32:53.721
Place, the Sharehouse bar.

32:53.805 --> 32:57.016
- Time, right now. Hostess, Choi I-ra.
- Choi I-ra is so funny. [chuckles]

32:59.852 --> 33:00.853
Are you going?

33:01.688 --> 33:03.648
I'm sure everyone would like to see you.

33:04.774 --> 33:06.317
Hmm… [chuckles]

33:07.110 --> 33:08.194
I can't.

33:11.030 --> 33:12.532
You were the one who said

33:12.615 --> 33:15.034
not to let anyone hurt me anymore,
didn't you?

33:15.868 --> 33:17.370
Later, when I thought about it,

33:17.954 --> 33:20.873
I realized that I mistreated myself
the most out of everyone.

33:23.501 --> 33:26.629
And that's why I shouldn't be
friends with you for now, okay?

33:28.339 --> 33:30.174
I'm still hurt, you see.

33:34.303 --> 33:35.221
But who knows?

33:35.304 --> 33:36.723
I hope one day when I see you,

33:36.806 --> 33:39.308
I won't feel as badly
and we can be friends again.

33:40.476 --> 33:42.603
I think I just need
a little time for now, you know?

33:44.188 --> 33:46.357
I hope that you understand, Won-Jun.

34:02.665 --> 34:05.251
Come on. You were imagining
a lot of things, weren't you?

34:05.334 --> 34:07.420
Or is it because you
don't have the balls to get angry?

34:09.338 --> 34:11.382
[Won-jun]
Wow, so much for you saying you're sorry.

34:13.176 --> 34:15.011
Do you even feel bad for what you did?

34:15.720 --> 34:17.472
I thought it wouldn't matter to me

34:17.555 --> 34:20.099
if you were just having a little fun
or taking a break,

34:20.183 --> 34:21.642
or if you were feeling lonely.

34:21.726 --> 34:23.770
I liked you,
and I thought I could handle it.

34:23.853 --> 34:25.521
I didn't care
if you had no feelings for me.

34:28.274 --> 34:30.443
And now I know
I can't handle this anymore.

34:30.526 --> 34:31.652
[sighs]

34:42.997 --> 34:43.831
[door opens]

34:46.167 --> 34:47.043
[door closes]

34:49.629 --> 34:50.630
You're moving out?

34:51.214 --> 34:52.465
[Won-jun] Yes.

34:52.548 --> 34:54.634
- [Doona] Where to?
- Well, I don't know yet.

34:55.802 --> 34:57.261
What if I begged you not to move out?

35:00.932 --> 35:03.017
- Do I really have to answer that?
- Yes, you do.

35:06.104 --> 35:06.938
[sighs]

35:09.273 --> 35:10.525
Would you please get out?

35:28.584 --> 35:31.796
- Let go of me. You smell like tobacco.
- [Doona] But I quit.

35:33.339 --> 35:34.507
It's probably his, then.

35:38.594 --> 35:40.096
So you're the jealous type, aren't you?

35:41.389 --> 35:42.473
What is it?

35:42.974 --> 35:44.433
Did he not want you anymore?

35:45.143 --> 35:46.519
Is that why you came back to me?

35:46.602 --> 35:48.813
Quit while you're ahead
and it's cute still.

35:53.818 --> 35:55.111
I'm not going anywhere.

35:56.112 --> 35:58.239
You'll have to drag me out of here
otherwise, huh?

35:58.322 --> 36:00.533
Listen, Doona,
I told you I don't want you in here!

36:00.616 --> 36:03.995
- So why can't you just leave me alone?
- 'Cause I want to be around someone.

36:04.078 --> 36:05.788
That doesn't have to be me.
I don't have to.

36:05.872 --> 36:06.706
You do have to.

36:08.040 --> 36:09.458
You have to be the one.

36:16.174 --> 36:17.175
Then, why did you do it?

36:19.302 --> 36:20.761
Because I didn't know that…

36:22.305 --> 36:24.599
that the person I didn't want to lose

36:25.975 --> 36:27.143
was you, okay?

36:30.354 --> 36:32.190
I don't have a lot of experience,

36:32.273 --> 36:35.359
and I'm even slower
when it comes to my own feelings.

36:36.903 --> 36:39.071
I take things for granted
until they're gone.

36:39.572 --> 36:40.948
And then I regret it.

36:42.074 --> 36:43.826
I can't help it. It drives me crazy.

36:45.745 --> 36:48.873
So why can't you, um,
forgive me just this once?

36:50.958 --> 36:53.419
You really are a mess. You know that?

36:54.128 --> 36:55.963
You're selfish and unstable, and

36:56.589 --> 36:58.883
you hurt me without even
thinking twice about it.

37:00.051 --> 37:01.552
I feel conflicted because

37:02.136 --> 37:04.722
you came and totally
flipped my world upside down.

37:05.389 --> 37:06.849
But even still, I feel like

37:08.309 --> 37:11.229
I'm going crazy because I want
to be the one that you want.

37:16.859 --> 37:18.653
So tell me you're really sorry.

37:23.366 --> 37:24.408
I'm sorry.

37:24.492 --> 37:25.952
And that I'm what you want.

37:27.453 --> 37:29.872
Tell me that you only have eyes for me
and not that guy!

37:33.084 --> 37:33.960
Can you?

37:37.213 --> 37:38.130
I love you.

37:39.840 --> 37:41.884
[emotional music playing]

38:08.786 --> 38:09.620
[Doona] Won-jun.

38:11.122 --> 38:11.956
[Won-jun] Hmm?

38:13.165 --> 38:14.834
[Doona] Please don't hate me.

38:15.918 --> 38:17.253
[Won-jun] I don't hate you.

38:18.754 --> 38:19.880
Believe me, I tried.

38:20.756 --> 38:22.133
But I just couldn't.

38:23.926 --> 38:25.344
[Doona] I don't mean now.

38:26.220 --> 38:27.388
I mean, going forward.

38:30.016 --> 38:31.434
[Won-jun] I promise I won't.

38:34.729 --> 38:36.439
[Doona] Does this mean we made up?

38:37.732 --> 38:38.649
[Won-jun] Mm-hmm.

38:40.067 --> 38:41.777
[Doona] Really? So easily?

38:43.070 --> 38:44.780
[Won-jun] I've always been easy.

38:44.864 --> 38:46.782
I was just pretending to be difficult.

38:50.119 --> 38:52.121
[emotional music continues]

38:56.709 --> 38:58.044
[Won-jun] It has to be you

38:58.586 --> 38:59.503
for me too.

39:06.927 --> 39:08.929
[Doona humming]

39:17.271 --> 39:21.317
[Doona] Do you remember the song
that I gave up writing halfway through?

39:21.817 --> 39:24.153
We were working
on our second album, I think.

39:24.236 --> 39:25.738
[humming]

39:26.572 --> 39:28.282
I had forgotten the melody,

39:29.950 --> 39:31.369
but it came back to me.

39:32.119 --> 39:33.788
[humming]

39:34.997 --> 39:36.916
- [woman] That's good.
- [Doona] It is.

39:36.999 --> 39:38.209
[both laughs]

39:38.876 --> 39:42.505
[Doona] I wonder if it came back to me
because I've been feeling happier.

39:47.385 --> 39:49.261
[woman] You should drink that.
You did order it.

39:49.762 --> 39:51.764
[gentle music playing]

40:11.617 --> 40:13.619
[crowd cheering]

40:17.665 --> 40:19.667
[gentle music continues]
